WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.092 --> 00:00:02.480
(upbeat music)

2
00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.240
If you have a not-so-green thumb like me,

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.780
you'll love this tip from a plant expert.

4
00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:10.690
Here's plant stylist, my favorite, Hilton Carter.

5
00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:11.730
You gotta take a look.

6
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:14.920
When you decide to water your plant, just like others,

7
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.460
you're gonna do it nice and easy,

8
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:20.170 line:15%
slow and steady around the entire pot,

9
00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:22.820 line:15%
making sure that every single root

10
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:26.660 line:15%
in there has a moment to pull in moisture.

11
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.030
That is important.

12
00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:32.720
And because you haven't watered this desert plant in weeks,

13
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.860
it's going to need to be watered completely through,

14
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.510
all the way through all the roots,

15
00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:39.780
and all the way down into your base tray.

16
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.610
Now we're talking about water.

17
00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.390
Water for the snake plant is one

18
00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:46.380
of the reasons people kill it.

19
00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:47.570
Overwatering.

20
00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:48.990
So you wanna be aware of that.

21
00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.330
Signs of an overwatered snake plant

22
00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.590 line:15%
is soft, yellowing tissue.

23
00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:54.660 line:15%
As you can see,

24
00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:59.610 line:15%
all of the tissue is turning very yellow and very mushy.

25
00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:01.200
And then when it leans like that,

26
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.360
that is a clear sign that it has been overwatered,

27
00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:05.870
and now it is dying.

28
00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:08.320
But an underwatered snake plant leaf

29
00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:12.250 line:15%
will show signs of just, let's say browning,

30
00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.200 line:15%
dry browning on the edge of the foliage.

31
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.130 line:15%
But if that happens,

32
00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:19.010 line:15%
what you can do here is you can kind of trim that off.

33
00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:20.290
You can use your nail, maybe.

34
00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:21.720
Trim that off, and there it is.

35
00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.890
It's gone, and now you still have the rest

36
00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:26.640
of your leaf looking great.

37
00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.300
But if you overwater,

38
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.920
there's nothing really you can do here.

39
00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.100
So once you see dying foliage happen like this,

40
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.800
this is probably a good time to start pruning

41
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:40.310
that plant back to at least give all of the foliage

42
00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:43.690
that still has good life in it the time,

43
00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:47.510
the moment to really grow, to really thrive.

44
00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:49.680
I need more Hilton Carter in my life.

45
00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.470
Chip and Joanna, where can I find him?

46
00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:53.620
Well, he hosts the Guide to Houseplants

47
00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:56.910
and Caring for Common Houseplants workshops

48
00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:57.960
on the Magnolia app,

49
00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.420
where you can grow your houseplant skills.

50
00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.477
Well, thumbs up for green thumbs.

51
00:02:02.477 --> 00:02:05.144 line:15%
(upbeat music)

